Dockerfile-la commonly important instructions:

Instruction	Purpose

FROM	- Base image
WORKDIR	- Working directory
COPY	- Copy files
ADD	- Copy/add files with extra behavior
RUN	- Build-time command
CMD	- Default container command
ENTRYPOINT	- Main executable/entrypoint
EXPOSE	- Document intended port
ENV	- Environment variable
ARG	- Build-time variable
USER	- Run as specific user
LABEL	- Image metadata
HEALTHCHECK -	Container health check


And:

.dockerignore

is also very important because it controls what gets sent in the Docker build context.
We'll go through these properly rather than memorizing a table.

🧠 One important mental model

When you see:

FROM node:22-alpine

WORKDIR /app

COPY package*.json ./

RUN npm ci

COPY . .

CMD ["npm", "start"]

Think:

FROM
↓
"What environment do I start with?"

WORKDIR
↓
"Where is my application?"

COPY
↓
"What files do I need?"

RUN
↓
"What should happen while BUILDING the image?"

CMD
↓
"What should happen when STARTING the container?"